{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Strange Coincidences", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Life's Strange", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 7, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 16, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe unusual events through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Simple Past", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about many kinds of past events: short, quickly finished actions, longer situations and repeated events.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Usually, when you use the Simple Past tense, the time of the finished action is clear from the context or explicitly mentioned in the sentence.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Yesterday, a robber <span class=\"strong\">stole</span> something like ten thousand dollars in cash.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Here is another example:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Ten minutes later, The robber <span class=\"strong\">came</span> back to the bank.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Remember that there are both regular and irregular verbs. Look at the chart for examples of the Simple Past tense verbs.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Regular Verbs</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discover\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"discovered\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognize\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"recognized\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Irregular Verbs</span>:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"know\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"knew\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "What happened?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Yesterday, he stole something like ten thousand dollars in cash and ran out the door.", "type": "example"}, {"content": " The teller filled the bag with money.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Present Perfect", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Present Perfect tense to talk about a past action or an action that began in the past that is connected to the present in some way. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You can use the Present Perfect tense to talk about experience.<br/>When you use the Present Perfect tense, you think about the past and present together. There is some connection between what happened in the past and now. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "For example: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I have learned English</span> = I learned English in the past and now I can speak English.<br/><span class=\"italic\">He has bought a painting</span> = He bought the painting in the past and now he has a painting. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "To emphasize the result of the action, use the simple form.<span class=\"italic\"><br/><br/><ul><li>Have you heard the latest news?</li><li>I haven't heard that story.</li></ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Have you ever heard a story that crazy before?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Have you heard that one?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I have heard a lot of strange stories, but that was the strangest.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Has there been a lot of bizarre stories in the news lately?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There has been a few.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hilarious", "type": "name"}, {"content": "extremely funny", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You are hilarious.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about a bank robbery.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "teller", "type": "name"}, {"content": "one who works in a bank to receive or pay out money over the counter", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You won't believe it, a man walked into a bank downtown and gave the bank teller a note.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nuts", "type": "name"}, {"content": "weird, crazy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Wow. That is nuts.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to get away", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to escape; flee", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(phrasal verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: So he got away?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "remorseful", "type": "name"}, {"content": "full of, or characterized by, deep and painful regret ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The remorseful bankrobber.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le16ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "can't wait", "type": "name"}, {"content": "used when you are excited about something to happen",